<!-- CASE C - the hypothesis: AS with precipitation and clogging active.

     This is the base deck plus the shared composition file, with nothing overridden:
       - AS fluid at saturation (Omega = 1) at the injection temperature
       - initialSurfaceArea = 100 m2/m3 in the rock, gated by damage (surfaceAreaDamageExponent=1)
         so reaction happens only in the fractured region
       - DamageCloggingPermeability, so precipitate closes the fracture down

     DRIVER: cooling. The base deck prescribes a radial temperature field, warm at the borehole and
     falling to rock temperature over a radius rc that grows from 7 to 27 mm across the run. The
     fluid enters at Omega = 1 and supersaturates as it cools, so precipitation tracks the cold
     zone. rc is derived from the injection rate in coolingField_tables/make_cooling_field.py and
     is the main thing to sweep: the 1D work showed that front position, not chemistry, sets where
     the plug forms, and that a front which moves too fast smears the deposit instead of plugging.

     Expected signature once the driver is in: precipitate accumulates where the thermal front
     sits, permeability collapses there, borehole pressure climbs above cases A and B, and the
     fracture branches rather than extending as a single plane.

     Kept as a separate file rather than running the base directly so that the case matrix is
     explicit and the base can gain shared changes without silently redefining "case C". -->
<Problem>
  <Included>
    <File name="./AS_wellbore_base.xml"/>
    <File name="./AS_wellbore_logConc.xml"/>
  </Included>
</Problem>
